\f1\fs22 He listened for a moment, and heard someone large, cumbersome and grumbling pass by.\
\'93Morning, Dr Logan,\'94 he heard that Stockwell man boom.\
Alexander gave it half a minute then snuck into the hall. \
He stopped when he saw Kathy through the next door, sitting on the bed, hands folded in her lap, head down. She looked up at him.\
\'93Wow,\'94 he said. \'93You look miserable.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Kathy laughed, and a tear lived a brief lifetime travelling down her cheek, contemplating the vicissitudes of gravity. \'93Sarah\'85\'94\
\'93Sarah: where is she?\'94\
Kathy looked away and chewed on her thoughts. \'93Following\'85\'94\
\'93Following? Who? I\'92m right here.\'94\
Kathy tried to stare through Alexander\'92s skull in search of brain cells. \'93She had Hayley put a gun to your head.\'94\
\'93I know! The ratings will be through the roof.\'94\
Kathy giggled and Alexander wondered if there was medication he should find for her. \
\'93She\'92s gone to work,\'94 Kathy said.\
\'93Work?\'94\
\'93I swear, she\'92ll give birth right there on the Ironing Room floor.\'94\
\'93She\'92s doing my ironing?\'94\
\'93Yes, Alexander, she\'92s starching your collars\'97and your underwear so it bulges the way you like. And right after that, she\'92ll try to stop your mother from blowing up the world.\'94\
\'93Ah, yes.\'94 Alexander had reclaimed some equilibrium. \'93She does lean on that tendency sometimes. I just hope I have a camera crew handy when it happens.\'94 He cast his eyes around the room. \'93Look. Can you tell me what department she works in?\'94\
Kathy shrugged, and told Alexander the colours to follow.\
He thanked her and disappeared from the doorway. A second later he was in the doorframe. \'93Hey, Kathykins. Go find Hayley. You look like you could use a cuddle.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

