\f1\fs22 He rushed; he hyperventilated like a finalist at a beauty pageant. A sense of self-preservation froze his feet to the floor. He gathered his breath and blinked away the madness. Well, most of it. He looked up and down the corridor and couldn\'92t decide whether the next junction was closer than the previous. He couldn\'92t think straight; he needed to calm down, so he pulled his device out and activated its camera. Holding it in landscape, he peered through, forward and back. His breathing eased as  he went ahead. 
